From 63bf301359257d877eef37eccfb891109aba9bdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:35:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: hold the first SC2 MPEG12 launch for a
 following unit

The SC2 MPEG12 MULTI firmware completes a picture only when it reaches
the next start code. Launching cold with only the first access unit
committed ends in DATA_EMPTY mid-picture. Every later cold replay from
ring offset 0 then fails to parse the leading sequence header again:
SEQ_INFO stays 0 and MPEG1_2_REG never gets its MPEG-2 bit. Decoding
recovers only at the next sequence header, so a whole GOP is lost.

Observed register state of the first launch and the replays was matched
(command/picture geometry, PIC_DC_CTRL bit 31, a reloaded TEE firmware
image) without changing that outcome. Do not start the first cold run
until a further unit is committed or EOS is queued. Payloads,
timestamps, buffer counts and DMA isolation are unchanged.

On the original 24-packet 1080i MPEG-2 input this returns 24 of 24
pictures for NV12/NV21 in and out, with LAST, EPIPE and EOS. Against an
independent software decode the maximum sample difference is 4. The
retained FFmpeg V4L2 MPEG-1 and MPEG-2 320x240 inputs return 36 of 36
with maximum differences 4 and 5.

Change-Id: I61a9bc5319a258d28566546acc1251aa5a069b1b
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
index 6f0216b18a84..e5032a317697 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_mpeg12.c
@@ -283,6 +283,7 @@ struct mpeg12_multi {
 	struct mutex lock;
 	struct list_head preroll;
 	u32 input_refs;
+	u32 first_end;
 	void *workspace;
 	dma_addr_t workspace_dma;
 	void *cc;
@@ -539,6 +540,14 @@ static int mpeg12_multi_run(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 	    (!m->swap_valid && !m->committed) ||
 	    (m->empty && m->job_end == m->committed))
 		return 0;
+	/* The MULTI firmware completes a picture only at the next start code.
+	 * A cold launch with just AU0 ends in DATA_EMPTY mid-picture, and every
+	 * cold replay from offset 0 then skips the leading sequence header until
+	 * the next one. Hold the first launch for a following unit or EOS.
+	 */
+	if (!m->swap_valid && !m->job_end && !m->eos_queued &&
+	    m->committed == m->first_end)
+		return 0;
 	for (i = 0; i < MPEG12_MULTI_BUFFERS; i++) {
 		if (i != m->refs[0] && i != m->refs[1] &&
 		    !m->picture[i].pending && !m->picture[i].displayed) {
@@ -989,6 +998,8 @@ static void mpeg12_multi_input_committed(struct amvdec_session *sess,
 
 	mutex_lock(&m->lock);
 	m->committed = offset + bytes;
+	if (!m->first_end)
+		m->first_end = m->committed;
 	ret = mpeg12_multi_run(sess);
 	if (ret)
 		m->error = ret;
